   Setup — this machine's logins and terminal

   kit welcome --checks --machine   ⧉   ▶️ 
   kit ran it once, as this screen opened; the checks below are what it found. ⧉ copies it, to run in your own shell,
   and ▶️ runs it again here.

   ❌ gh is not logged in to github.com
      gh auth login --hostname github.com · it needs you at the keyboard
   ❌ kit check finds 2 differences from the release
      read: kit help check

   This step checks what the work on this machine needs. It checks the command-line tool of the code forge kit reaches,
   GitHub's gh, and your login there. In a terminal, it also judges the terminal kit runs in, and names each of its
   settings that makes kittui slower or worse.

   When a check fails, the line under it gives the command that fixes it, or says where to read more. Run the command
   yourself, or have kit run it and check again. kit runs nothing until you ask. A terminal's fixes are yours to make
   in its settings, so kit shows them and never runs them, and keep holds a finding as it is.

   A check drawn 💡 is an offer: it holds, and you can leave it. This guide checks the machine alone, and knows no
   repository or workspace. Inside a repository, kit welcome --text also checks each folder of its workspace: kit
   installed, its files placed, the git hooks, the tools and linters, and kit check. For how kit finds the folders,
   read docs/workspaces.md (https://github.com/empowerite/kit/blob/main/docs/workspaces.md).












